### Page 1 of 4

```text
ORDINANCE NO. ________

ENTITLED: "AN
ORDINANCE
AMENDING
VARIOUS
SECTIONS
WITHIN
CHAPTER 8.12, INTERNATIONAL FIRE CODE ADOPTED, OF TITLE 8,
HEALTH AND SAFETY, OF THE MUNICIPAL CODE OF THE CITY OF
CHEYENNE, WYOMING, UPDATING THE EDITION OF THE
INTERNATIONAL FIRE CODE ADOPTED BY THE CITY AND
FURTHER AMENDING AS SPECIFIED."

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That Chapter 8.12, International Fire Code Adopted, is amended as follows:

8.12.010 - Purpose—Authority—General provisions.

The purpose of this chapter is to adopt the International Fire Code, 2018 2021 Edition, as an
enforceable regulation governing the safeguarding of life and property from fire and explosion
hazards arising from the storage, handling and use of hazardous substances, materials, and devices,
and from conditions hazardous to life or property in the occupancy of buildings and premises.

8.12.020 - International Fire Code—Adopted.

A document, being marked and designated as provided in this section and one copy of which one
copy is on file in the office of the city clerk and open for inspection of the public, in the office of
the city clerk, being marked and designated as is adopted and made a part hereof as if fully set out
in this chapter:

International Fire Code, 2018 2021 Edition, as published by the International Code
Council, Inc., including Appendices A, B, C, D, E, F, G and I; through N.
is referred to, adopted and made a part hereof as if fully set out in this chapter.

8.12.030 - Amendments.

The International Fire Code adopted in Section 8.12.020 above is amended as follows:

A. Section 101.1. insert: The City of Cheyenne; for [NAME OF JURISDICTION].

B. Section 102.1 is amended by adding subsection 5 as follows:

5.4.  In making a determination whether a particular structure, facility or condition
constitutes a distinct hazard, the fire code official shall follow the guidelines and
procedures specified for Section 102.1.4 which appear on page 1-8 of in the official
commentary to the 2018 2021 Edition of the International Fire Code.

10:04 am, Dec 14, 2022
```

### Page 2 of 4

```text
Page 2 of 4

C. Section 110.4 is deleted and re-created to read as follows: 103.1 insert: Cheyenne Fire
Rescue; for [NAME OF JURISDICTION].
Penalties shall be as specified in Section 1.24.010 of the Cheyenne City Code.

D. Section 112.4 is deleted and re-created to read as follows: insert: misdemeanor, for
[SPECIFY OFFENSE]; insert seven hundred fifty dollars ($750.00) and costs, for
[AMOUNT]; and insert period not to exceed one hundred eighty (180) days, for
[NUMBER OF DAYS].

Penalties shall be as specified in Section 1.24.010 of the Cheyenne City Code.

E. Section 607.2 606.2 is amended by the addition of one exception to read as follows:

Exception: Day care Commercial facilities that utilize residential stovetops need not
provide a Type I or Type II hood, subject to all of the following:

1.a.
The equipment is used for warming or limited cooking only, no frying is
permitted and a permanent sign is posted stating "No Cooking Creating Grease
Laden Vapors Permitted"; and

2.b.
A 2A-10BC fire extinguisher is placed in the kitchen; and

3.c.
Approval of the exception is provided, in writing, by the city fire code
official.

F. Section 903.2.8 is amended to read as follows:
903.2.8 Group R. An automatic sprinkler system installed in accordance with
Section 903.3 shall be provided throughout all buildings with a Group R fire area.

Exception: Three or more dwelling units in a structure need not be provided with an
automatic sprinkler system when all the following provisions are met:

1. Each dwelling unit has its primary exit directly to the exterior of the structure.

2. Each structure does not exceed 2 stories (levels) in height.

3. Each structure is provided with a fire wall complying with Section 706 that
separates not more than 2 dwelling units.

Buildings containing not more than 4 dwelling units, which are not separated by fire
walls, shall comply with Section 903.3 subject to all of the following provisions:

1. All sprinkler systems shall comply with a design approved by the City of Cheyenne
Fire and Rescue Department.
```

### Page 3 of 4

```text
Page 3 of 4

2. All sprinkler systems shall have an approved back flow preventor and a water
control valve installed.

3. The minimum domestic water tap will be 1½ inch for 3 or 4 unit buildings. The fire
line may come off the domestic line.

4. Properly licensed plumbing contractors will be permitted to install residential
sprinkler systems in structures containing not more than 4 dwelling units.

Buildings containing 5 or more dwelling units, which are not separated by fire walls,
shall be provided with an automatic sprinkler system installed in accordance with Section
903.3. In either case Section 508.5.1 shall apply, with a maximum of 600 foot of hose lay.

G.F.
Section 5504.3.1.1.3 is amended to read as follows:

Location. Stationary containers shall be located in accordance with Section 3203.6.
Containers of cryogenic fluids shall not be located within diked areas containing other
hazardous materials. The storage of flammable cryogenic fluids in stationary containers
outside of buildings is prohibited in all areas other than heavy industrial (HI) zone areas,
only with the approval of, and under conditions established by, the fire chief code official.

H.G. Section 5608.10, disposal, is deleted and re-created as follows

Any shells found during the inspection required in Section 5608.9 shall not be handled
until at least 15 minutes have elapsed from the time the shells were fired. The disposal
instructions of the manufacturer as provided by the fireworks supplier shall be followed in
disposing of the fireworks in accordance with Section 5604.10.

I.H.
Section 5704.2.9.6.1 is amended to read as follows:

The storage of Class I and Class II liquids in above-ground tanks stationary containers
outside of buildings shall be as specified in city code Section 8.24.020.

J.I. Section 5706.2.4.4 is amended to read as follows:

The storage of Class I and Class II liquids in above-ground tanks stationary containers
shall be as specified in city code Section 8.24.020.

K.J.
Section 5806.2 is amended to read as follows:

The storage of flammable cryogenic fluids in stationary containers outside of buildings
shall be as specified in city code Section 8.24.020.

